# Universe content · cities, buildings and infrastructure
# researched: urban morphology study guides (organic, grid, radial, linear, clustered, networked layouts);
#   UCL thesis on planned and organic cities; settlement-pattern geography notes (dispersed, linear, nucleated);
#   Gottmann's "megalopolis"
# Cities are generated live, in the builder species' own image (LAW 14). The 100 grouping steps are on
# the public Groups & Flocking page.
# Spec: docs/CONTENT-FORMAT.md · wiki/systems/r09-civilization.md · wiki/systems/r04b-generators.md

# ── Settlement sizes ──

@settlement camp
name: Camp
real: yes
says: a temporary group of shelters

@settlement hamlet
name: Hamlet
real: yes
says: a handful of homes

@settlement village
name: Village
real: yes
says: homes and farms around a center

@settlement town
name: Town
real: yes
says: a market, workshops and a few hundred to thousands of people

@settlement city
name: City
real: yes
says: a dense center of trade, rule and belief

@settlement metropolis
name: Metropolis
real: yes
says: a huge city that leads a whole region

@settlement megalopolis
name: Megalopolis
real: yes
says: cities grown together into one endless urban chain

@settlement ecumenopolis
name: Planet-city
real: hypothetical
says: a whole world covered by one city

@settlement arcology
name: Arcology
real: hypothetical
says: a whole city inside one giant building

# ── Layouts ──

@layout organic
name: Organic layout
real: yes
says: no plan; narrow winding streets that follow the land; old cities

@layout grid
name: Grid layout
real: yes
says: straight streets crossing at right angles; planned cities

@layout radial
name: Radial layout
real: yes
says: streets spreading like spokes from a central square

@layout linear
name: Linear layout
real: yes
says: a long town along one river, road or coast

@layout clustered
name: Clustered layout
real: yes
says: tight groups of buildings with open land between

@layout networked
name: Networked layout
real: yes
says: many centers joined by transport lines

@layout walled
name: Walled layout
real: yes
says: a ring of walls with the city packed inside

@layout concentric
name: Concentric rings
real: yes
says: rings of districts around an old core, newer rings outside

