# ── Generator rules ──

@rule city-seed
real: rule
says: every settlement, building and road is generated live; nothing is pre-built

@rule city-own-image
real: rule
says: cities follow the builder species' body plan and genes: insect species build hive cities of segmented cells, burrowers build underground, fliers build tall towers and roosts, swimmers build reef and underwater cities, giants build huge, small species build dense

@rule city-grows
real: rule
says: a settlement climbs the 100 grouping steps (camp, hamlet, village, town, city…), growing districts and infrastructure as it goes

@rule city-age
real: rule
says: the civilization's age decides its materials and infrastructure, from mud and paths to composites and spaceports

@rule city-terrain
real: rule
says: cities grow along rivers, coasts and trade routes; hills get defenses; layouts bend around the land

@rule city-society
real: rule
says: the city's society shapes it: temples tower in theocracies, palaces in monarchies, factories in industrial economies (100 kinds of society)

@rule city-conditions
real: rule
says: on hostile worlds cities need the tech for every world condition: domes, shielded roofs, floating platforms (the 10 × 10 world matrix)

@rule city-fall
real: rule
says: collapsed civilizations leave ruins that decay and can be resettled
